// Pixel size of a face at a zoom: half-points are 1/144 in and a pixel is 1/96 in, so px = hp * zoom / 150 rounded to nearest; unset sizes (-1) take quill_layout_font_size and super/sub text (bits 16 and 32) takes quill_layout_script_percent percent of its size first. Kept within the 1..512 the font layer accepts.
// By hand: 24 hp at 100 = 2400 / 150 = 16 px; at 150 = 24 px; 48 hp is 32 px; 24 hp as a superscript is 24 * 58 / 100 = 13 hp, (1300 + 75) / 150 = 9 px.
face_pixel_size(int pixel_half_points, int bits, int zoom) {
  if(pixel_half_points < 0) {
    pixel_half_points = (import quill_layout_font_size);
  }
  if((bits & 48) != 0) {
    pixel_half_points = pixel_half_points * (import quill_layout_script_percent) / 100;
  }
  int pixel_count = fixed_point_maximum(fixed_point_minimum((pixel_half_points * zoom + 75) / 150, 512), 1);
} return int pixel_count;
(24, 0, 100):(16)
(24, 0, 150):(24)
(48, 0, 100):(32)
(-1, 0, 100):(16)
(24, 16, 100):(9)
(24, 32, 100):(9)
(1, 0, 100):(1)
(9999, 0, 100):(512)

